/* ============================================================================
   matrix-add.epher -- add two 3x3 matrices

   Matrices add entry by entry, (A + B)[r][c] = A[r][c] + B[r][c] (any linear
   algebra text, e.g. Strang, "Introduction to Linear Algebra", 5th ed.,
   sec. 1.3). The built-in + does exactly that. The two matrices below are
   reverses of each other, so every entry of the sum is 10; subtracting B
   again returns A, which the last boolean checks. All values are exact.

   Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/algebra/matrices/matrix-add.epher"

   The knobs to edit are the matrices A and B below.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs ---------------------------------------------------------------
const A = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]
const B = [[9, 8, 7], [6, 5, 4], [3, 2, 1]]

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
A + B                             // A + B, entry by entry (echoes the sum)
print("(A + B) - B brings back A:", (A + B) - B == A)
/* ---- expected output ----
= [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]
= [[9, 8, 7], [6, 5, 4], [3, 2, 1]]
= [[10, 10, 10], [10, 10, 10], [10, 10, 10]]
= (A + B) - B brings back A: true
*/
